                "a": "(1) Prime factors of 36 = 2 x 2 x 3 x 3\nPrime factors of 54 = 2 x 3 x 3 x 3\nCommon factors = 2, 3, 3\nProduct of common factors = 2 x 3 x 3\n= 18\nNon-common factors = 2, 3\nProduct of non-common factors = 2 x 3\n= 6\nLCM = 18 x 6\n= 108\n(2) Prime factors of 33 = 3 x 11\nPrime factors of 55 = 5 x 11\nCommon factors = 11\nProduct of common factors = 11\nNon-common factors = 3, 5\nProduct of non-common factors = 3 x 5\n= 15\nLCM = 11 x 15\n= 165\n(3) Prime factors of 52 = 2 x 2 x 13\nPrime factors of 78 = 2 x 3 x 13\nCommon factors = 2, 13\nProduct of common factors = 2 x 13\n= 26\nNon-common factors = 2, 3\nProduct of non-common factors = 2 x 3\n= 6\nLCM = 26 x 6\n= 156\n(4) Prime factors of 16 = 2 x 2 x 2 x 2\nPrime factors of 24 = 2 x 2 x 2 x 3\nPrime factors of 40 = 2 x 2 x 2 x 5\nCommon factors = 2, 2, 2\nProduct of common factors = 2 x 2 x 2\n= 8\nNon-common factors = 2, 3, 5\nProduct of non-common factors = 2 x 3 x 5\n= 30\nLCM = 8 x 30\n= 240\n(5) Prime factors of 27 = 3 x 3 x 3\nPrime factors of 48 = 2 x 2 x 2 x 2 x 3\nPrime factors of 72 = 2 x 2 x 2 x 3 x 3\nCommon factors = 3\nProduct of common factors = 3\nNon-common factors = 2, 2, 2, 2, 3, 3\nProduct of non-common factors = 2 x 2 x 2 x 2 x 3 x 3\n= 144\nLCM = 3 x 144\n= 432\n(6) Prime factors of 50 = 2 x 5 x 5\nPrime factors of 80 = 2 x 2 x 2 x 2 x 5\nPrime factors of 90 = 2 x 3 x 3 x 5\nCommon factors = 2, 5\nProduct of common factors = 2 x 5\n= 10\nNon-common factors = 2, 2, 2, 3, 3, 5\nProduct of non-common factors = 2 x 2 x 2 x 3 x 3 x 5\n= 360\nLCM = 10 x 360\n= 3600\n(7) Prime factors of 56 = 2 x 2 x 2 x 7\nPrime factors of 84 = 2 x 2 x 3 x 7\nPrime factors of 98 = 2 x 7 x 7\nCommon factors = 2, 7\nProduct of common factors = 2 x 7\n= 14\nNon-common factors = 2, 2, 3, 7\nProduct of non-common factors = 2 x 2 x 3 x 7\n= 84\nLCM = 14 x 84\n= 1176\n(8) Prime factors of 44 = 2 x 2 x 11\nPrime factors of 66 = 2 x 3 x 11\nPrime factors of 99 = 3 x 3 x 11\nCommon factors = 11\nProduct of common factors = 11\nNon-common factors = 2, 2, 3, 3\nProduct of non-common factors = 2 x 2 x 3 x 3\n= 36\nLCM = 11 x 36\n= 396\n(9) Prime factors of 25 = 5 x 5\nPrime factors of 50 = 2 x 5 x 5\nPrime factors of 75 = 3 x 5 x 5\nCommon factors = 5, 5\nProduct of common factors = 5 x 5\n= 25\nNon-common factors = 2, 3\nProduct of non-common factors = 2 x 3\n= 6\nLCM = 25 x 6\n= 150\n(10) Prime factors of 15 = 3 x 5\nPrime factors of 25 = 5 x 5\nPrime factors of 30 = 2 x 3 x 5\nPrime factors of 45 = 3 x 3 x 5\nCommon factors = 5\nProduct of common factors = 5\nNon-common factors = 2, 3, 3, 5\nProduct of non-common factors = 2 x 3 x 3 x 5\n= 90\nLCM = 5 x 90\n= 450\n(11) Prime factors of 10 = 2 x 5\nPrime factors of 20 = 2 x 2 x 5\nPrime factors of 32 = 2 x 2 x 2 x 2 x 2\nPrime factors of 40 = 2 x 2 x 2 x 5\nCommon factors = 2\nProduct of common factors = 2\nNon-common factors = 2, 2, 2, 2, 5\nProduct of non-common factors = 2 x 2 x 2 x 2 x 5\n= 80\nLCM = 2 x 80\n= 160\n(12) Prime factors of 12 = 2 x 2 x 3\nPrime factors of 24 = 2 x 2 x 2 x 3\nPrime factors of 48 = 2 x 2 x 2 x 2 x 3\nPrime factors of 54 = 2 x 3 x 3 x 3\nCommon factors = 2, 3\nProduct of common factors = 2 x 3\n= 6\nNon-common factors = 2, 2, 2, 3, 3\nProduct of non-common factors = 2 x 2 x 2 x 3 x 3\n= 72\nLCM = 6 x 72\n= 432"
