                "q": "Look at the figure and answer the following:\nIn the figure, AOC is a straight line, O is a point on it, and OE and OD are two rays from O on the same side of AOC.\n(i) Is ∠AOE adjacent to ∠DOE?\n(ii) Is ∠AOD adjacent to ∠COD?\n(iii) Is ∠AOE adjacent to ∠AOD?\n(iv) Is ∠DOE adjacent to ∠EOC?",
                "a": "(i) Yes.\n∠AOE and ∠DOE have the common vertex O and the common arm OE, and OA and OD lie on opposite sides of OE.\n(ii) Yes.\n∠AOD and ∠COD have the common vertex O and the common arm OD, and OA and OC lie on opposite sides of OD.\n(iii) No.\n∠AOE and ∠AOD have the common vertex O and the common arm OA, but OE and OD lie on the same side of OA, so the angles overlap.\n(iv) No.\n∠DOE and ∠EOC have the common vertex O and the common arm OE, but OD and OC lie on the same side of OE, so the angles overlap."
