                "a": "(i) The hypotenuse is the side opposite the right angle at C.\nHypotenuse = AB = about 3.6 cm.\n(ii) The hypotenuse is the side opposite the right angle at Q.\nHypotenuse = PR = about 3.6 cm.\n(iii) The hypotenuse is the side opposite the right angle at X.\nHypotenuse = YZ = about 3.8 cm.\n(iv) The hypotenuse is the side opposite the right angle at N.\nHypotenuse = LM = about 3.9 cm.\n(v) The hypotenuse is the side opposite the right angle at E.\nHypotenuse = DF = about 4.0 cm.\n(vi) The hypotenuse is the side opposite the right angle at I.\nHypotenuse = GH = about 4.0 cm."
