                "q": "Using a ruler and protractor to construct the following triangles. Measure the length of remaining two sides and one angle of the triangle.\n(i) ΔABC, mAB = 5 cm, m∠BAC = 55°, m∠ABC = 35°\n(ii) ΔJKL, m∠KJL = 65°, m∠JKL = 25°, mJK = 4.8 cm\n(iii) ΔPQR, m∠QPR = 30°, m∠PQR = 60°, mQP = 4 cm\n(iv) ΔSTU, mST = 5.3 cm, m∠STU = 75°, m∠TSU = 15°",
                "a": "(i) Third angle, m∠ACB = 180° − 55° − 35°\n= 90°\nRemaining sides: mBC = about 4.1 cm and mAC = about 2.9 cm.\n(ii) Third angle, m∠JLK = 180° − 65° − 25°\n= 90°\nRemaining sides: mKL = about 4.4 cm and mJL = about 2.0 cm.\n(iii) Third angle, m∠PRQ = 180° − 30° − 60°\n= 90°\nRemaining sides: mQR = 2 cm and mPR = about 3.5 cm.\n(iv) Third angle, m∠SUT = 180° − 75° − 15°\n= 90°\nRemaining sides: mTU = about 1.4 cm and mSU = about 5.1 cm."
