              {
                "q": "Use protractor, a pair of compasses and ruler to construct the following triangles:\n(i) Acute angled ΔABC, m∠BAC = 65°, mAB = 3.6 cm, mAC = 4.4 cm\n(ii) Right angled ΔDEF, m∠DEF = 90°, mDF = 3 cm, mEF = 4 cm\n(iii) Obtuse angled ΔLMN, m∠NML = 110°, mMN = mML = 5 cm\n(iv) Acute angled ΔPQR, m∠PQR = 60°, mPQ = mQR = 4 cm\n(v) Right angled ΔXYZ, m∠XYZ = 90°, mXY = 4.2 cm = mYZ\n(vi) Obtuse angled ΔSTU, m∠STU = 120°, mST = 3.6 cm, mTU = 4.2 cm",
                "a": "(i) Draw AB = 3.6 cm.\nAt A, draw ∠BAC = 65° with a protractor.\nMark C on the ray so that AC = 4.4 cm.\nJoin BC.\nΔABC is the required acute angled triangle.\n(ii) This triangle cannot be constructed.\nIn a right angled triangle, the hypotenuse is the longest side.\nHere the hypotenuse DF = 3 cm is shorter than the side EF = 4 cm.\nSo no such triangle exists.\n(iii) Draw ML = 5 cm.\nAt M, draw ∠NML = 110° with a protractor.\nMark N on the ray so that MN = 5 cm.\nJoin LN.\nΔLMN is the required obtuse angled triangle.\n(iv) Draw PQ = 4 cm.\nAt Q, draw ∠PQR = 60° with a protractor.\nMark R on the ray so that QR = 4 cm.\nJoin PR.\nΔPQR is the required acute angled triangle.\n(v) Draw XY = 4.2 cm.\nAt Y, draw ∠XYZ = 90° with a protractor.\nMark Z on the ray so that YZ = 4.2 cm.\nJoin XZ.\nΔXYZ is the required right angled triangle.\n(vi) Draw ST = 3.6 cm.\nAt T, draw ∠STU = 120° with a protractor.\nMark U on the ray so that TU = 4.2 cm.\nJoin SU.\nΔSTU is the required obtuse angled triangle."
              }
