                "a": "(i) No.\nTwo right angles add up to 180°.\nThe third angle would be 0°, which is not possible.\n(ii) Yes.\nFor example, a triangle with angles 60°, 60° and 60° has two acute angles.\n(iii) No.\nTwo obtuse angles add up to more than 180°.\nThe sum of the three angles would be more than 180°, which is not possible.\n(iv) No.\nIf each angle is less than 60°, the sum of the three angles is less than 180°.\nBut the angles of a triangle must add up to exactly 180°.\nSo it is not possible."
