                    "a": "Friendly microbes are very important for human beings and the environment: bacteria in the soil break down garbage and the remains of living organisms into simple nutrients, which make the soil fertile and helpful for plant growth; some bacteria and fungi help in the digestion of food; yeast is used for raising bread and some bacteria are used in making yogurt, cheese and sour cream; microbes produce antibiotics such as penicillin and vaccines such as polio drops; and they are also used in the making of leather and detergent powders.",
                    "q": "These are friendly microbes. Do you know how they are important for human beings and the environment?"
