                    "a": "Dengue is a disease caused by the bite of one kind of mosquito. The mosquito contains a virus called dengue virus. When the mosquito bites a human, it transfers the virus into the human body. The diseased person develops high fever, skin rash and sometimes may bleed. The mosquito causing dengue thrives in fresh water ponds.\nWays to fight dengue: do not let fresh water collect and stand in ponds, pots, tyres and other containers around the home; keep the surroundings clean; cover water containers; use mosquito nets and take care to avoid mosquito bites; and keep the environment clean so that harmful microorganisms do not grow.",
                    "q": "The people of the Province of Sindh, Pakistan, are facing a serious problem these days. Many people are developing a disease called Dengue. The diseased person develops high fever, skin rash and sometimes may bleed. Doctors explain: Dengue is a disease caused by the bite of one kind of mosquito. The mosquito contains a virus called dengue virus. When the mosquito bites a human, it transfers the virus into the human body. The mosquito causing dengue thrives in fresh water ponds. The community is thinking of solutions to fight dengue. Can you help in coming up with some solutions?"
