                    "a": "Meteoroids are small rocky, stony and metallic debris (pebble to several meters) in a variety of orbits; they burn up in the atmosphere and are seen as meteors or shooting stars. Asteroids are rocky objects from a few meters up to several hundred meters, mostly in the asteroid belt between Mars and Jupiter; they are sometimes called planetoids. Comets are small bodies of ice, dust and rock (dirty snowballs) with a nucleus and a coma, moving in highly elongated orbits and forming a long tail near the Sun.",
                    "q": "Compare meteoroids, asteroids and comets."
